DrawingML: keep the model identity of theme hyperlink colors

The programmatic hlink color choice set the color token but not its name.
Character-property conversion uses that name for complex theme colors.
Set both, as the XML color parser does, so export keeps schemeClr=hlink.
Explicit tx colors are untouched; no original XML is replayed.

diff --git a/oox/source/drawingml/textrun.cxx b/oox/source/drawingml/textrun.cxx
index 1160e36..3b5fb48 100644
--- a/oox/source/drawingml/textrun.cxx
+++ b/oox/source/drawingml/textrun.cxx
@@ -160,7 +160,10 @@ sal_Int32 TextRun::insertAt(
                 xTextFieldCursor->gotoEnd( true );
 
                 if (!maTextCharacterProperties.maHyperlinkPropertyMap.hasProperty(PROP_CharColor))
+                {
                     aTextCharacterProps.maFillProperties.maFillColor.setSchemeClr(XML_hlink);
+                    aTextCharacterProps.maFillProperties.maFillColor.setSchemeName(u"hlink"_ustr);
+                }
 
                 aTextCharacterProps.maFillProperties.moFillType = XML_solidFill;
                 if ( !maTextCharacterProperties.moUnderline.has_value() )
